{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":"2026-09-18T09:00:47.933Z","tool_name":"invoke_agent","tool_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d5d1a6d1b608f64","parameters":{"agent_name":"generalist","prompt":"HAC DATABASE QUERY for Jira ticket GMT-21241 — Three cronjobs in ABORTED status on SMI/MENA Hybris platform.\n\nThe three cronjobs are:\n1. toko-iq-ecom-flat-c360-reports\n2. full-backofficeIndex-CronJob\n3. kwMktCPIProductCategoryOutboundSyncCronJob\n\nRun the following FlexibleSearch queries using hac-direct.cjs (located at C:\\toko\\toko6\\toko6\\core-customize\\hybris\\bin\\hac-direct.cjs). Run each as a separate `node hac-direct.cjs \"QUERY\"` command. The proxy env var prefix for the command is: `$env:NO_PROXY=\"devops.sdsdev.co.kr,sdsdev.co.kr,aipro.sdsdev.co.kr,nexus.sdsdev.co.kr,teams.microsoft.com,*.teams.microsoft.com,*.microsoft.com,login.microsoftonline.com,*.onecdn.static.microsoft,*.static.microsoft,teams.public.onecdn.static.microsoft\"; $env:NPM_CONFIG_PREFIX=\"\"`\n\nQuery 1: Get cronjob details for all 3 cronjobs:\n```\nSELECT {c.code}, {c.jobCode}, {c.status}, {c.active}, {c.singleExecutable}, {c.logLevel}, {c.result}, {c.startTime}, {c.endTime}, {c.lastActivationTime}, {c.abortRequested}, {c.sessionId}, {c.nodeId}, {c.errorMode}, {c.queryPage}\nFROM {CronJob AS c}\nWHERE {c.code} IN ('toko-iq-ecom-flat-c360-reports','full-backofficeIndex-CronJob','kwMktCPIProductCategoryOutboundSyncCronJob')\n```\n\nQuery 2: Get cronjob status history (from JobLog records):\n```\nSELECT {jl.cronJob_code}, {jl.status}, {jl.message}, {jl.creationtime}\nFROM {JobLog AS jl}\nWHERE {jl.cronJob_code} IN ('toko-iq-ecom-flat-c360-reports','full-backofficeIndex-CronJob','kwMktCPIProductCategoryOutboundSyncCronJob')\nORDER BY {jl.creationtime} DESC\n```\nNote: JobLog may not have a direct relation to cronJob code. If the above fails, try:\n```\nSELECT {jl.cronjob}, {jl.status}, {jl.message}, {jl.creationtime}\nFROM {JobLog AS jl}\nWHERE {jl.cronjob} IN (\n  SELECT {c.pk} FROM {CronJob AS c}\n  WHERE {c.code} IN ('toko-iq-ecom-flat-c360-reports','full-backofficeIndex-CronJob','kwMktCPIProductCategoryOutboundSyncCronJob')\n)\nORDER BY {jl.creationtime} DESC\n```\n\nQuery 3: Get the trigger information for these cronjobs:\n```\nSELECT {t.cronJob}, {t.active}, {t.activationTime}, {t.cronExpression}, {t.maxAcceptableLateness}\nFROM {Trigger AS t}\nWHERE {t.cronJob} IN (\n  SELECT {c.pk} FROM {CronJob AS c}\n  WHERE {c.code} IN ('toko-iq-ecom-flat-c360-reports','full-backofficeIndex-CronJob','kwMktCPIProductCategoryOutboundSyncCronJob')\n)\n```\n\nQuery 4: Get the cronjob's associated job (the JobPerformable bean):\n```\nSELECT {c.code}, {j.code}, {j.springId}\nFROM {CronJob AS c JOIN Job AS j ON {c.job} = {j.pk}}\nWHERE {c.code} IN ('toko-iq-ecom-flat-c360-reports','full-backofficeIndex-CronJob','kwMktCPIProductCategoryOutboundSyncCronJob')\n```\n\nQuery 5: Check if there are any ongoing/running cronjobs that might conflict:\n```\nSELECT {c.code}, {c.status}, {c.startTime}\nFROM {CronJob AS c}\nWHERE {c.status} IN (1, 2) \n```\nNote: Status 1 = RUNNING, 2 = PAUSED. Also try with string values: WHERE {c.status} = 'RUNNING'\n\nQuery 6: Check cluster node info for where these cronjobs last ran:\n```\nSELECT {c.code}, {c.nodeId}, {c.sessionId}, {c.lastActivationTime}\nFROM {CronJob AS c}\nWHERE {c.code} IN ('toko-iq-ecom-flat-c360-reports','full-backofficeIndex-CronJob','kwMktCPIProductCategoryOutboundSyncCronJob')\n```\n\nReturn ALL raw output from each query. Do NOT summarize. Include every column and row.","wait_for_previous":false}}
